 or when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transform"},{"type":"text","text":" throws an error."}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this method to receive a single-level asynchronous sequence when your"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transformation produces an asynchronous sequence for each element."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In this example, an asynchronous sequence called "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" produces "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"values from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"5"},{"type":"text","text":". The transforming closure takes the received "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and returns a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" that counts that high. For example, when the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transform receives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":" from the base sequence, it creates a new "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Counter"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that produces the values "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"1"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"2"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"flatMap(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“flattens” the resulting sequence-of-sequences into a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncSequence"},{"type":"text","text":". However, when the closure receives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"4"},{"type":"text","text":", it throws an"},{"type":"